          "note": "Three compatibility fixes and a couple of UI improvements.\n\nThis release is a collection of some UI improvements, compatibility\nenhancements and a bit of work to make content in this repo easy to import and\nreuse in the new  https://llama-swap.ai website.\n\nThanks to everyone who filed detailed bugs and contributed changes. The\nquality of this project would not be where it is without the community.\n\n----\n\n- [1249e7c](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/commit/1249e7c8b53b56dcb079a117fe1aa8ab5fa414cb) changelog: make into package: makes `changelog/` an importable Go package with `Versions()`, `Latest()` and `Get()` over the embedded per-release markdown so llama-swap.ai can display the release notes by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1315](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1315) ui: reduce ActivityTable render rate: throttles the Activity table to one render every 125 ms and skips redraws while the inflight panel is hidden, because live token/duration counters repainted on every update and burned CPU whenever several streams were active by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1318](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1318) UI: category and a capability badge for decision models: gives models declaring the `decision` capability their own sidebar/list category and a matching badge, since categories were derived from capabilities but decision models fell through with neither by [@sousekd](https://github.com/sousekd)\n- [PR #1319](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1319) internal/server: pass through 1xx interim responses in recorders: forwards 1xx statuses without recording them, because `Expect: 100-continue` (sent by curl for bodies over about 1 MiB) made the recorders latch onto the relayed `100 Continue` and discard the real status, so upstream 400/500 errors arrived at the client as 200 by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1326](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1326) Remove metadata filtering to allow custom fields alongside capabilities: stops dropping `architecture`, `capabilities`, `supported_parameters`, `context_length` and `context_window` from user `metadata` when capabilities are set, since that metadata is nested under `meta.llamaswap` and cannot collide with the generated top-level fields by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1327](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1327) Add autoload=false support to /props endpoint: answers `GET /props?autoload=false` with 409 instead of loading a model that is not running (as llama-server's router mode does), so clients like llama.vscode that probe every listed model no longer load them one after another and evict the loaded model by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)",
          "cut_from": null
        }
